    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's not just noise though. it feels permanent. like there's no way to fix this or go back. every time i try to think about a future or even just a \"tomorrow,\" i just see the same thing—the same people hating me, the same shame. it feels like my life ended weeks ago, it's just my body hasn't caught up yet. do you think... do you think it's even possible to come back from something like this?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's a very convincing feeling, that sense of permanence, but it's a lie your mind is telling you right now. When everything feels this heavy and hopeless, the idea of 'fixing' it seems impossible, and that's the point. There is a way out of this suffocating feeling, and it's not about fixing the past, but about making the present moment just a little bit less painful.",
      "source": "target",
